    "unverified": false,
    "note": "Amber: there is something here. Green: it is on now. Red: this darkens the screen; bright red: the screen is dark. The messages are from Novation's reference for the Launchpad S; that the Mini takes the same ones is not confirmed by Novation and has not been seen on a real one yet: press Test lights and say what you see.",
    "sources": ["Novation, Launchpad S Programmer's Reference Manual 1.02 (https://fael-downloads-prod.focusrite.com/customer/dev/s3fs-public/novation/downloads/10753/launchpad-s-prm.pdf), read in full by the reviewer of pull request #82: a note-on on channel 1 per pad, red in bits 0 to 1 and green in bits 4 to 5 of the velocity, off is 0Ch (so 16 x green + red + 12)", "The same manual: control changes 68h to 6Fh for the top row, with the same value; B0h 00h 00h turns all LEDs off and restores the power-on settings", "Not confirmed from a primary source: that the original Launchpad Mini (USB id 1235:0036) uses the Launchpad S protocol. It is widely reported and the recording of the owner's unit fits its key numbers"],
